        "src/tests/installer_profile_workflow.test.py:20-32,40-59,124-163",
        "src/tests/installer_export_conflict.test.py:38-96",
        "src/tests/installer_desired_profile.test.py:219-251"
      ],
      "detail": "The test named reviewed_desired_yaml_reaches_both_consumers_and_concrete_plan explicitly selects components=[] and accepts either render exit 0 or 2, checking only that an artifact exists. The nonempty LeRobot real-entry test exports actual YAML and asserts local render success but does not check Ansible rendering, and its plan assertion is only exit 2 plus the component ID substring. The conflict suite has a nonempty local positive control but serializes JSON-exported profile itself rather than exercising YAML-format export. Pure Ansible export coverage exists separately. These are useful complementary controls, not proof that one current nonempty reviewed artifact passes both renderers with exact selected sources/runtimes/targets and no unintended mutation.",
      "recommended_boundary": "For any separately authorized verification, use a deliberately supported nonempty selection, require actual nonempty shared YAML and exact both-renderer mappings, preserve all negative/unsupported gates, and assert exact concrete plan statuses plus execution_authorized=false. This recommendation does not authorize a run now."
    },
