      ],
      "detail": "The confined profile path resolves and renders/plans, never imports managed_apply, and always sets execution_authorized=false. Target observation is explicit only and emits managed=false. Existing mkdir targets can be satisfied; existing enabled component repositories/artifacts remain blocked, not automatically adopted. Bundled/Conda runtimes retain unresolved-runtime-prefix labels without separate prefix evidence; shared schema does not admit fixture_local/path/managed_files shortcuts. Thus a nonempty robotics plan can correctly return exit 2 with concrete repository targets and explicit runtime unknowns. Do not make it all-satisfied by importing managed fixtures, fabricating ownership, deleting selected actions or weakening assertions. If no-change means no mutation, verify that boundary separately; if it means zero proposed changes/full conformance, the current scoped path does not establish that."
